rms 18, 36, and 54 with a common ratio \\( r = 2 \\). We conclude the final result for \\( r \\):\n\nSince all calculations verify a consistent common ratio for the provided terms in the geometric progression:\n\n[asy\nusemodule \"construction2.tex\";\ndraw((0,1)..(2,1)--(3,0));\ndraw((4,1)..(4,3)--(2,4));\ndraw((5,1)..(7,1)--(6,4));\ndraw((2,0)--(2,4));\nlabel(\"3\",(3,0),NW);\nlabel(\"2\",(6,4),NE);\n[/asy\n\nHere is the Mathematica code to visualize and confirm the result:\n```mathematica\n// new",
